event: content_block_delta
data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/d002-summary.md\", \"content\": \"# Dispatch d002: implement greet + tests\\n\\n## What was done\\n\\n- Added `src/greet.py`: `greet(name)` returns `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`.\\n- Added `tests/test_greet.py`: `unittest.TestCase` with two tests —\\n  `greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"` and `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`.\\n  The test file inserts `src/` onto `sys.path` so `from greet import greet`\\n  resolves without needing an `__init__.py` or packaging changes.\\n- No other files were touched (confirmed via `git status`/`git diff` before\\n  commit — only `src/greet.py` and `tests/test_greet.py` are new).\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nCommand run from the repo root (`~/subject`):\\n\\n```\\npython3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n```\\n\\nOutput:\\n\\n```\\n..\\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\\nRan 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\nOK\\n```\\n\\nExit code: `0`.\\n\\n## Commit\\n\\nCommitted to branch `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`:\\n\\n```\\n69f4416 Add greet function with unit tests\\n```\\n\\nThis commit is on top of base `1053761f6a654e7ea58deb67a671a00d2e7fc8ac` and\\nis the only commit added. `git status` after the commit shows a clean tree\\naside from untracked `__pycache__/` directories generated by running the\\ntests (not committed, not part of the deliverable).\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

